    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let us examine the conversation line by line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Что с телефонами?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What's with your phones?' Back at the restaurant, a rattled Max asks why neither Kostya nor Nastya answered their phones.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Я не могу дозвониться.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I can't get through.' He complains that he has been trying to reach them all morning.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Мой телефон украли.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'My phone was stolen.' Kostya explains that somebody stole his phone while he was out.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nastya",
      "t": "Мне звонила мама.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Mom called me.' Nastya joins them and says her mother just called with news.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nastya",
      "t": "Папа познакомился с Костей.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Dad met Kostya.' She happily reports that her father finally met 'Kostya' at the apartment.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nastya",
      "t": "Но он думает, что это ты.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'But he thinks it's you.' Turning to Max, Nastya realizes her dad actually met Max by mistake. Then Max replies.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Я не понял.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I don't get it.' Max plays dumb for a second as the realization sinks in.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nastya",
      "t": "Он думает, что ты — Костя.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'He thinks that you are Kostya.' Nastya spells it out: her terrifying father now believes Max is her boyfriend Kostya.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Зачем он приходил?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Why did he come?' Max asks why her father showed up at the apartment in the first place.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Он угрожал мне.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'He threatened me.' Speaking from experience, Max notes that the man threatened him.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Скажи ему правду.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Tell him the truth.' Max begs Nastya to call her father and tell him the truth about who is who.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nastya",
      "t": "Я не могу.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I can't.' Nastya shakes her head and says she cannot do that.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nastya",
      "t": "Он очень жестокий.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'He is very cruel.' She admits that her father has a fierce, unforgiving temper.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Что же мне делать?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What should I do?' Trapped in the mix-up, Max despairs over what he is supposed to do now. Now let's listen to the whole conversation again from start to finish.",
